# .gitignore
# vim: set tabstop=4 shiftwidth=4 expandtab:

# NOTE: do not copy the public dib7 .gitignore over this one. That tree ignores
# vaults/* and local/*, but in this repo both are tracked on purpose: the vault
# files are ansible-vault encrypted, and local/ holds the site scripts. Ignoring
# them here would silently drop any newly added vault or local script.
#
# Keeping vaults out of the public tree is handled by the --exclude flags in
# local/rsync-to-dib7.sh, not by this file. rsync copies from the filesystem and
# never consults .gitignore.

# Editor and OS cruft
*~
.*.sw[op]
.vscode/
.DS_Store

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Ansible
*.retry

# Image build artifacts, in case build_dir is ever pointed inside the repo.
# These run to tens of GB; committing one by accident is painful to undo.
*.mf
*.ova
*.ovf
*.qcow2
*.raw
*.vmdk

# Left behind by older versions of local/rsync-to-dib7.sh
elements-save/

# Lock file bin/publish-image-catalog.py creates beside the catalog. Empty and
# per-machine, so only the lock is ignored: catalogs/image-catalog.json is
# tracked here on purpose, which is what gives it history and a backup. It names
# this site's AMIs, GCP projects and vSphere content libraries, so it stays out
# of the public tree - local/rsync-to-dib7.sh excludes it there.
catalogs/image-catalog.json.lock
